# Cheaper guest-memory tracking per draw (26 Nov). The profile put the tracker phase at 0.40 us a draw, up from 0.23
# before upload hoisting (0102): marking a range read wrote one stamp per 4 KB page, 256 of them for a 1 MB vertex
# buffer, on every draw that requested it. Now the read marks are a bitmap (64 pages a word, with a per-word
# generation so nothing is cleared between submissions). And MemorySync::Request keeps a small memo of ranges found
# current: the same range again, with no invalidation since, skips the valid-bit checks, and within one submission
# also the read marking. BOTS_GFX_TRACKER_MEMO=0 turns the memo off. The hitch log line now counts memo hits.
